## Deliverable
```
# Design Specification: Atlas Core Dashboard Density Reduction
Author: Fig Reyes, Design Agent
Working Style: Data Purist
Status: Approved for Engineering

## 1. Overview & Objectives
Following layout performance audits on Atlas Core, dashboard cognitive load scores exceeded baseline targets by 28%. This spec establishes streamlined spatial tokens, card component margins, and selective telemetry display to improve data ingestion rates across both SaaS Platform metrics and Face to Face Services management views.

## 2. Resource Utilization
- **Business Document: Company Document**: Analyzed to align density reduction parameters with enterprise reporting mandates, statutory SaaS telemetry retention requirements, and cross-departmental KPI visibility standards without omitting required compliance indicators.

## 3. Spatial & Density Token Updates
```json
{
  "tokens": {
    "spacing": {
      "card-padding-default": "16px",
      "card-padding-compact": "12px",
      "grid-gap": "16px",
      "section-margin-bottom": "24px"
    },
    "typography": {
      "metric-value-size": "28px",
      "metric-label-size": "12px",
      "secondary-text": "11px"
    },
    "elevation": {
      "card-shadow": "0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.06)",
      "border-stroke": "1px solid var(--border-subtle)"
    }
  }
}
```

## 4. Key Modifications
1. Metric Card Simplification: Collapsed multi-line micro-charts into sparkline components with on-hover telemetry drill-down.
2. Grid Hierarchy: Converted 6-column fragmented metric grids into a 4-column prioritized key-metrics layout.
3. Table Row Height: Standardized data grid row heights to 40px (down from variable 48-64px padding) with increased contrast ratios for enhanced readability.
```